# AdLift

**AdLift** is an original, portfolio-quality ad click prediction and ranking demonstration inspired by the recommender-system theme of NVIDIA Merlin Models.

---

## Project Overview

- **Goal**: Predict whether an ad impression will receive a click, evaluate models honestly, and serve predictions through a FastAPI service and a local interactive dashboard.
- **Important Scope**:
  - The dataset supports **click prediction on observed impressions**.
  - A ranking demo may sort supplied candidate records by predicted score, but **it must not claim to have proved that showing the top-ranked ad would cause more clicks** (the offline observational data does not provide an online counterfactual experiment).
  - Explicit prevention of target leakage: post-impression conversion events (`conversion`, `conversion_timestamp`, etc.) and outcome counters (`click_pos`, `click_nb`) are strictly excluded from model inputs.

---

## Observed Dataset Schema

Direct inspection of `data/raw/criteo_attribution_dataset.tsv.gz` reveals 22 tab-separated columns:

| Column | Observed Type | Category / Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `timestamp` | `int64` | Context / Chronological order (seconds) |
| `uid` | `int64` | Hashed user identifier |
| `campaign` | `int64` | Hashed campaign identifier |
| `conversion` | `int64` | Post-impression conversion outcome (**Excluded**) |
| `conversion_timestamp`| `int64` | Post-impression conversion timestamp (**Excluded**) |
| `conversion_id` | `int64` | Post-impression conversion ID (**Excluded**) |
| `attribution` | `int64` | Attribution status (**Excluded**) |
| **`click`** | `int64` | **Target Label (0 or 1)** |
| `click_pos` | `int64` | Click position (-1 if no click) (**Leakage - Excluded**) |
| `click_nb` | `int64` | Click count (-1 if no click) (**Leakage - Excluded**) |
| `cost` | `float64` | Impression cost |
| `cpo` | `float64` | Cost per order / bid target |
| `time_since_last_click`| `int64` | Recency feature in seconds (-1 if first/none) |
| `cat1` - `cat9` | `int64` | Categorical context / feature hashes |

---

## Project Structure

```text
AdLift/
├── data/
│   ├── raw/                 # Ignored by git: criteo_attribution_dataset.tsv.gz
│   ├── processed/           # Ignored by git: intermediate splits & processed data
│   └── demo/                # Synthetic candidate impressions for ranking demo
│       └── synthetic_candidates.json
├── docs/                    # Architecture notes and feature specifications
│   └── features.md          # Step 3 detailed column categorization and leakage policy
├── reports/                 # Evaluation figures, comparison tables, and metrics
│   ├── figures/                         # Ignored by git: calibration, distribution, score bucket plots
│   ├── data_inspection_summary.json     # Step 2 chunked inspection report
│   ├── data_split_summary.json          # Step 4 chronological split diagnostics
│   ├── baseline_validation_metrics.json # Step 5 baseline validation metrics
│   ├── model_comparison.json            # Step 6 & 8 4-model validation metrics
│   ├── model_comparison.md              # Step 6 & 8 formatted comparison table
│   ├── calibration_and_error_analysis.json # Step 7 calibration metrics and slices
│   └── calibration_and_error_analysis.md   # Step 7 calibration and failure report
├── scripts/
│   ├── inspect_head.py          # Quick CLI inspection tool for compressed TSV
│   ├── inspect_data.py          # Streaming chunked inspection tool (configurable limit)
│   ├── create_splits.py         # Chronological train/validation/test split generator
│   ├── train_baselines.py       # Baseline models trainer and evaluator
│   ├── train_tabular.py         # Stronger LightGBM model trainer and comparator
│   ├── train_pytorch.py         # Step 8 PyTorch EmbeddingMLP trainer and comparator
│   ├── evaluate_calibration.py  # Calibration curves, score buckets, and slice analysis
│   └── demo_ranking.py          # Step 9 candidate ranking demonstration CLI
├── src/
│   └── adlift/
│       ├── __init__.py          # Package entry point
│       ├── analysis.py          # Calibration curve, slice diagnostics, and plot generator
│       ├── api/
│       │   ├── __init__.py      # API package entry
│       │   ├── app.py           # FastAPI service (/health, /predict, /rank)
│       │   └── schemas.py       # Pydantic request and response schemas
│       ├── data_loader.py       # Safe streaming chunk loader and schema profiler
│       ├── features.py          # Feature categorization, allowlist, and leakage validator
│       ├── models/
│       │   ├── __init__.py      # Models package entry
│       │   ├── baselines.py     # Constant and Logistic Regression baselines
│       │   ├── lightgbm_model.py # Regularized LightGBM tabular click model
│       │   └── pytorch_model.py # Compact PyTorch EmbeddingMLP click model
│       ├── ranking.py           # Step 9 deterministic candidate ranking & tie-breaker
│       ├── schema.py            # Raw schema definitions and constants
│       └── split.py             # Chronological partitioning and overlap diagnostics
├── tests/
│   ├── test_analysis.py         # Calibration and slice diagnostic tests
│   ├── test_api.py              # FastAPI endpoint (/health, /predict, /rank) & parity tests
│   ├── test_basic.py            # Basic structure, schema, and packaging tests
│   ├── test_baselines.py        # Baseline probability, reload, and metric tests
│   ├── test_data_loader.py      # Unit tests for chunked loader with synthetic fixture
│   ├── test_features.py         # Leakage prevention and feature allowlist tests
│   ├── test_lightgbm.py         # LightGBM probability, reload, and comparison tests
│   ├── test_pytorch.py          # PyTorch forward pass, training, and reload tests
│   ├── test_ranking.py          # Step 9 candidate ranking, tie-breaking, and validation tests
│   └── test_split.py            # Chronological invariant and split stability tests
├── pyproject.toml               # Project dependencies and packaging
├── README.md                    # Project documentation
└── .gitignore                   # Strict ignore rules for data, models, and caches
```

