## Setup & Verification on Windows PowerShell

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.9+ (or [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/))
- The raw dataset file placed at:
  ```text
  data/raw/criteo_attribution_dataset.tsv.gz
  ```

### 1. Environment Setup (using `uv`)
```powershell
# Create virtual environment and install dependencies
uv venv
uv pip install -e .
```
*Or using standard Python:*
```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -e .
```

### 2. Inspect Dataset Head (Step 1 Verification)
To view the real schema and the first 3 rows directly from the compressed file without decompression:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/inspect_head.py --rows 3
```

### 3. Streaming Chunked Data Inspection (Step 2 Verification)
Inspect 100,000 rows in safe chunks (25k rows per chunk) without loading the whole dataset into RAM:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/inspect_data.py --limit 100000
```

### 4. Generate Chronological Splits (Step 4 Verification)
Generate reproducible chronological train (70k), validation (15k), and test (15k) splits:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/create_splits.py --limit 100000
```

### 5. Train & Evaluate Baselines (Step 5 Verification)
Train Constant Baseline and regularized Logistic Regression on train split and evaluate on validation split:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/train_baselines.py
```

### 6. Train Stronger Tabular Model & Compare (Step 6 Verification)
Train regularized LightGBM tabular model and output the 3-model experiment comparison table:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/train_tabular.py
```

### 7. Evaluate Calibration & Diagnostic Slices (Step 7 Verification)
Generate reliability diagrams, score bucket tables, and recency/bid performance slices:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/evaluate_calibration.py
```

### 8. Train PyTorch Deep Learning Model (Step 8 Verification)
Train the compact PyTorch EmbeddingMLP model and update the 4-model comparison table:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/train_pytorch.py
```

### 9. Candidate Ranking Demonstration (Step 9 Verification)
Score and rank synthetic candidate impression records with deterministic tie-breaking:
```powershell
uv run python scripts/demo_ranking.py
```

### 10. Start and Test the FastAPI Service (Step 10 Verification)
Start the production-ready FastAPI service:
```powershell
uv run uvicorn adlift.api.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```
In a second PowerShell window, test the endpoints using native PowerShell commands:
```powershell
# 1. Health check probe
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:8000/health" -Method Get | ConvertTo-Json

# 2. Score impression records
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict" -Method Post -InFile "data/demo/example_predict_request.json" -ContentType "application/json" | ConvertTo-Json

# 3. Rank candidate ads with deterministic tie-breaking
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:8000/rank" -Method Post -InFile "data/demo/example_rank_request.json" -ContentType "application/json" | ConvertTo-Json
```

### 11. Run Full Test Suite
```powershell
uv run pytest
```
